    "keyNotes": "• The Shape of the Earth: An oblate spheroid (slightly flattened at the poles and bulging at the Equator).\n• Proofs of Earth's Sphericity:\n  - Circumnavigation of the earth without falling off an edge.\n  - Ship's visibility at sea (mast appears before hull when approaching shore).\n  - Curved circular shadow cast on the moon during lunar eclipses.\n  - Sunrise and sunset times vary eastward across the globe.\n  - High-altitude aerial and satellite photographs from space.\n• Earth Motions:\n  - Rotation: Spins on its axis once every 24 hours from west to east; causes day and night, deflections of wind (Coriolis effect), and 1 hour time difference per 15° of longitude.\n  - Revolution: Orbits the sun in an elliptical path every 365¼ days; causes the four seasons, varying lengths of day and night, and changing midday sun altitude.\n• Internal Structure: Crust (Lithosphere: SIAL and SIMA), Mantle (Asthenosphere), and Core (Barysphere: outer liquid, inner solid NIFE - Nickel and Iron).",
