    "keyNotes": "• Three Major Rock Classes:\n  1. Igneous Rocks: Formed from the cooling and solidification of molten magma/lava.\n     - Plutonic / Intrusive: Cools slowly deep inside the crust forming large crystals (e.g. Granite, Gabbro).\n     - Volcanic / Extrusive: Cools rapidly on the earth surface forming fine crystals (e.g. Basalt, Pumice, Obsidian).\n  2. Sedimentary Rocks: Formed from accumulated, stratified sediments deposited in layers and compacted over millions of years.\n     - Mechanically formed (Sandstone, Shale, Clay).\n     - Organically formed (Limestone, Coal, Peat).\n     - Chemically formed (Rock salt, Gypsum). Contain fossils!\n  3. Metamorphic Rocks: Pre-existing rocks fundamentally altered by intense heat, extreme pressure, or both.\n     - Granite becomes Gneiss; Limestone becomes Marble; Shale becomes Slate; Sandstone becomes Quartzite.\n• Economic Importance in Ghana: Building stones (granite quarrying), industrial minerals (limestone for cement at Buipe), precious mineral hosts (Birimian gold belts).",
