    "keyNotes": "• Economic Planning: Deliberate governmental formulation of economic targets and resource allocation to achieve accelerated growth over a specified period.\n  - Types of Plans: Short-term annual budgets, Medium-term plans (3–5 years, e.g. Coordinated Programme of Economic and Social Development Policies in Ghana), Long-term perspective plans (e.g. 40-Year Development Plan by NDPC).\n• The National Development Planning Commission (NDPC):\n  - Established under Articles 86 and 87 of Ghana's 1992 Constitution to advise the President and prepare coordinated national development frameworks.\n• International Financial Institutions:\n  - International Monetary Fund (IMF): Established at Bretton Woods (1944). Provides short-to-medium term balance of payments support, promotes exchange rate stability, and enforces macroeconomic conditionalities (e.g. Ghana's 17 IMF bailout programs).\n  - World Bank Group (IBRD & IDA): Provides long-term concessional loans, technical assistance, and grants for structural capital projects (roads, schools, dams, electrification).\n  - African Development Bank (AfDB): Regional multilateral bank financing African infrastructure and regional integration.",
