    "keyNotes": "• The Final Week:\n  - Triumphal Entry (Palm Sunday): Jesus enters Jerusalem riding a humble colt/donkey, fulfilling Zechariah 9:9 as the peaceful Prince of Peace.\n  - The Last Supper: Institute the New Covenant in His body (bread) and blood (wine); models servant leadership by washing his disciples' feet.\n  - Gethsemane Agony: Intense emotional struggle; submits his human will completely to the Father: \"Not my will, but yours, be done.\" Betrayed by Judas Iscariot with a kiss.\n• The Trials:\n  - Jewish Religious Trial before Sanhedrin (Caiaphas): Condemned for blasphemy when he affirmed being the Christ, the Son of God.\n  - Roman Political Trial before Pontius Pilate: Falsely accused of treason (forbidding tribute to Caesar and claiming to be a king). Pilate finds him innocent but yields to mob pressure to release Barabbas.\n• Crucifixion & Resurrection:\n  - Died on the Cross at Golgotha (Calvary); Seven Last Words; veil of the temple torn in two from top to bottom (direct access to God).\n  - Resurrected on the third day; tomb discovered empty by Mary Magdalene; commissioned disciples to preach the Gospel to all nations.",
