    "keyNotes": "• Meaning of Government:\n  - As an Institution of the State: The machinery or agency through which the will of the state is formulated, expressed, and attained. Comprises the Legislature, Executive, and Judiciary.\n  - As an Art or Process of Governing: The laying down and implementation of rules, policies, and laws to maintain social order and peace.\n  - As an Academic Discipline: The systematic study of political institutions, power relations, political theories, and international relations.\n• Essential Characteristics of the State:\n  1. Permanent Population: A defined group of people living together.\n  2. Defined Territory: Well-demarcated geographical boundaries including land, airspace, and territorial waters.\n  3. Government: An administrative apparatus to maintain internal order.\n  4. Sovereignty: Supreme, independent legal authority free from external control.\n• State vs. Nation: A State is a legal-political entity; a Nation is a cultural-psycho-social community sharing common ancestry, language, and cultural traditions.",
