    "isVip": true,
    "keyNotes": "• The Rule of Law (A.V. Dicey):\n  1. Supremacy of the Law: Absolute supremacy of regular law as opposed to arbitrary power or discretionary prerogative.\n  2. Equality before the Law: All citizens, regardless of social status, wealth, or political rank, are equally subject to the ordinary law of the land.\n  3. Protection of Fundamental Human Rights: Civil liberties are guaranteed and safeguarded by independent courts.\n• Separation of Powers (Baron de Montesquieu):\n  - The three organs of government (Legislature, Executive, Judiciary) must be separated in personnel, functions, and powers to prevent tyranny and despotism.\n• Checks and Balances:\n  - Each organ is equipped with constitutional powers to check and limit the abuses of the other organs (e.g. Presidential veto over bills; Parliament vetting ministerial nominees and approving budgets; Judiciary exercising Judicial Review to nullify unconstitutional laws).",
