    "keyNotes": "• Decentralization Concept: Devolution of political, administrative, and fiscal powers from the central national government to local sub-national assemblies.\n• Structure of Local Government in Ghana (1992 Constitution & Local Governance Act, 2016):\n  - Metropolitan Assemblies (Population > 250,000, e.g. AMA, KMA, STMA).\n  - Municipal Assemblies (Population > 95,000).\n  - District Assemblies (Population > 75,000).\n  - Sub-structures: Urban/Zonal/Town/Area Councils and Unit Committees.\n• Composition of MMDAs:\n  - 70% of members elected directly by universal adult suffrage on a non-partisan basis.\n  - 30% of members appointed by the President in consultation with traditional authorities and interest groups.\n  - The District Chief Executive (DCE/MCE): Nominated by the President and approved by at least two-thirds of assembly members present and voting.\n• Financing Local Government:\n  - District Assemblies Common Fund (DACF): Constitutional provision (Article 252) allocating not less than 5% of total national revenue to assemblies for local development.\n  - Internally Generated Funds (IGF): Property rates, market tolls, license fees.",
