    "isFreeTrial": false,
    "isVip": true,
    "keyNotes": "• Origins & Evolution of the Commonwealth:\n  - Evolved from the gradual dismantling of the British Empire as former colonies attained independence while retaining voluntary association with Britain.\n  - Modern Commonwealth: Established by the London Declaration of 1949, dropping allegiance to the British Crown as a condition for membership (republics like Ghana could join).\n  - Head of the Commonwealth: King Charles III (symbolic and ceremonial head).\n• Organizational Structure:\n  - Commonwealth Heads of Government Meeting (CHOGM): Held biennially in different member states to deliberate on international peace, trade, and climate action.\n  - Commonwealth Secretariat: Administrative headquarters in Marlborough House, London, headed by the Commonwealth Secretary-General.\n  - Commonwealth Ministerial Action Group (CMAG): Protects democratic values and suspends military regimes (e.g. Nigeria suspended in 1995; Zimbabwe suspended in 2002).\n• Core Principles & Values (Harare Commonwealth Declaration, 1991):\n  - Commitment to multi-party democracy, the rule of law, fundamental human rights, gender equality, and sustainable socio-economic development.\n• Benefits to Member Nations (Ghana):\n  - Education & Training: Commonwealth Scholarship and Fellowship Plan enabling thousands of Ghanaians to pursue postgraduate studies abroad.\n  - Technical Assistance: Commonwealth Fund for Technical Cooperation (CFTC) providing experts in finance, agriculture, and public administration.\n  - Sports & Cultural Diplomacy: The Commonwealth Games held every four years to foster friendship among member nations.\n  - Electoral Observation: Dispatching expert missions to monitor and certify democratic elections.",
